Umbriel keeps a fullscreen column clear of its neighbours past a panel (gemini-pda-mainline, MIT).

Upstream-ready message:

  layout/scrolling: reserve the exclusive zones beside a fullscreen column

  A fullscreen member of the scrolling strip is presented against the
  whole output, anchored to its column, while the strip lays columns out
  inside the usable area. The strip reserved the struts a fullscreen or
  maximize-to-edges window overhangs, but not the layer-shell exclusive
  zones a fullscreen window also covers. With a panel on the left, a
  fullscreen column to the right of the focused one therefore started
  the panel's width early and drew a band of itself over the focused
  column's side of the output (it is in the fullscreen tree, above the
  tiles).

  Reserve the exclusive zones along the strip as part of a fullscreen
  column's bleed, as the struts already are. The workspace passes them
  to the layout at each arrange and to drag previews. The covering
  scroll offset is unchanged, since presentation and the strip use the
  same column origin, so a focused fullscreen window still covers the
  output exactly.

Seen on a Gemini PDA (owner, 2026-11-14): qutebrowser fullscreen, focus moved to foot, a band of
about 50 px of the browser at the output's right edge, in the composited frame.

